@inproceedings{Coe:2016aa,
	abstract = {In this paper, we present a numerical toolbox for design-response analysis of wave energy converters (WECs).
The ``WEC Design Response Toolbox (WDRT)'' was developed during a series of efforts to better understand
and improved the WEC survival design process. The WDRT has been designed as a tool for researchers and
developers, enabling the straightforward application of statistical and engineering methods needed for design
response analysis of a WEC, including characterization of environmental extremes, extreme response statistics,
fatigue analysis and design wave composition. This paper gives a brief overview of the WDRT including its
capabilities and underlying theory.},
